{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And the flesh of the sacrifice of his peace-offering of thanksgiving.</b> There are many inclusives here — to include the sin-offering, the guilt-offering, the ram of the nazirite, and the festal offering of the fourteenth, that they are eaten for a day and a night (Sifra)." "<b>On the day of his offering it shall be eaten.</b> The time for its flesh is the time for its bread." "<b>He shall leave none of it until morning.</b> But he may eat all night. If so, why did they say until midnight? To keep a person far from transgression (ibid.)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:21.329006068Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}